  "name": "KETONE BODY (BETA HYDROXYBUTYRATE) SERUM**",
  "code": "1126",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<p data-start=\"226\" data-end=\"264\"><strong data-start=\"226\" data-end=\"264\">Purpose and Clinical Significance:</strong></p>\n<ul data-start=\"265\" data-end=\"734\">\n<li data-start=\"265\" data-end=\"367\">\n<p data-start=\"267\" data-end=\"367\">Measures <strong data-start=\"276\" data-end=\"307\">beta-hydroxybutyrate (&beta;-HB)</strong>, the most abundant ketone body in the blood during ketosis.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"368\" data-end=\"509\">\n<p data-start=\"370\" data-end=\"509\">Used primarily to <strong data-start=\"388\" data-end=\"440\">diagnose and monitor diabetic ketoacidosis (DKA)</strong>, especially in cases of insulin deficiency or uncontrolled diabetes.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"510\" data-end=\"627\">\n<p data-start=\"512\" data-end=\"627\">Superior to urine ketone tests, as it reflects real-time ketone production and correlates with severity of ketosis.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"628\" data-end=\"734\">\n<p data-start=\"630\" data-end=\"734\">Also useful in assessing <strong data-start=\"655\" data-end=\"733\">starvation states, alcoholic ketoacidosis, and inborn errors of metabolism</strong>.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th><strong>Beta-Hydroxybutyrate Level</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Possible Clinical Indications</strong></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Elevated</strong></td>\n<td>Diabetic ketoacidosis (DKA), prolonged fasting/starvation, ketogenic diet, alcoholism, pregnancy ketosis, inborn errors of metabolism (e.g., fatty acid oxidation disorders)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Normal</strong></td>\n<td>No significant ketone production; excludes ongoing ketosis or acidosis related to ketone buildup</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>",
